For `pthread_rwlock_trywrlock()`, the specified error is **`EBUSY`** when the read-write lock is already locked for reading or writing—including when it is already owned by the calling thread.

`EDEADLK` is specified for `pthread_rwlock_wrlock()`, not `pthread_rwlock_trywrlock()`, in the cited POSIX specification. Therefore, for a nonblocking attempt to acquire an already-held write lock, test for:

```c
int ret = pthread_rwlock_trywrlock(&lock);

if (ret == EBUSY) {
    /* Lock is already held for reading or writing. */
}
```

The results may be undefined if the lock is uninitialized.
